{
  "_howto": "Everything about where every family's military currently is -- the 'changes constantly' tier (unlike places.json, which are the never/rarely-changes tiers and no longer carry a fleets field at all). Two categories: 'stationed' = anonymous fleets sitting at a body right now, no identity, never move on their own (bodyId + fleets array of owner names) -- supported but no longer auto-seeded; every family now starts with real NAMED fleets instead (see below). 'fleets' = NAMED, orderable fleets, now grouped into an object keyed by owner family name (each value an array of that family's fleets, owner no longer repeated per-fleet) -- give one an id (unique, kebab-case) and a chronological 'orders' list mixing move/disable/enable entries: {month, action:'move', target} where target is a body id, another fleet's id (fleet-vs-fleet intercept), or the literal 'home'; or {month, action:'disable'} / {month, action:'enable'}. A move order's month is the EARLIEST possible departure, not a fixed one -- arrival is never authored, it's solved as a real intercept problem against the target's live/orbiting position using the fleet's own 'speed' (AU/month, defaults to 4 if omitted). 'maxDistance' (AU, same unit as speed, null/omitted = uncapped) caps how far a single order can travel in one leg -- if the target isn't reachable within that range yet, the fleet WAITS in place (still tracked live at wherever it's parked) until the first month it comes into range, then departs; only flagged in the family overlay if no in-range launch window is ever found. Before its first order a named fleet sits at its owner's home planet, UNLESS it has an optional 'startBody' field naming a different body id to start at instead. Between orders it holds wherever the last one resolved it to; disable/enable mark an inactive (ghosted) window without deleting the fleet, and any move order whose month falls inside one is inertly skipped. SPEED/MAXDISTANCE/BONUSRANGE/BONUS: a fleet just names a 'type' (one of the archetype keys in strategic-map.js's FLEET_ARCHETYPES -- currently 'interceptor', 'suppressor', 'ground-support', 'arcanic-shield') and gets that archetype's speed/maxDistance/bonusRange/bonus for free -- no need to fill these in per fleet any more. 'bonusRange' (AU, separate from maxDistance) is how far from its OWN home planet a fleet can be while its 'bonus' (free-text, shown on a planet's info panel while the fleet is parked there, informational only) still counts as active -- the map computes and shows this live (Bonus attivo/inattivo). A 'legendary'/special fleet can still override any one of these four fields by just writing it directly on the fleet -- its mere presence (even set to null/'') wins over the archetype's default for that field only; the 4 fleets with unique hand-written bonus text (lunicaflotta, rivera-originale, shawel-crociata, ousssek-flotta-1) do this and have no 'type' at all. Fleet count is no longer might-capped -- generating a new fleet is a roleplay/dice action (see script.js's 'Genera Flotta'), not something this file enforces a limit on.",
